            <ArticleTitle>[A man who is not able to straighten his knee].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A9856</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An 86-year-old man presented at the Emergency Department with pain in his right leg and the inability to extend his knee after a fall. An ultrasound of the leg revealed a quadriceps tendon rupture. Surgical repair was performed and we expect complete recovery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
